<h2>Segment 230 &mdash; worlds as products of conception</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s230S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w1"><span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s230m1">rigs pa</span> drug cu pa</span> las <span class="u particle" data-d="6" data-l="s230p1">kyang</span> , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p0">&#x27;jig rten ma rig rkyen can du</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w5">gang phyir</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w6">rdzogs pa&#x27;i sangs rgyas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w7">gsungs</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p2">de yi phyir na</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w8">&#x27;jig rten &#x27;di</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w9">rnam rtog</span> yin <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p3">zhes cis mi &#x27;thad</span>, , <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p4">ces gsungs pa&#x27;i don</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w10">&#x27;grel par</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w11">&#x27;jig rten rnams</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w12">rang gi ngo bos</span> ma grub pa <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p5">rtog pas btags pa tsam du</span> bshad cing</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s230S">The <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w1">Sixty Verses on <span class="u" data-d="7" data-l="s230m1">Reasoning</span></span> say <span class="u particle" data-d="6" data-l="s230p1">as well</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p0">The world is something that ignorance causes</span>; <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w5">Why?</span> For the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w6">Buddhas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w7">say</span> it is so. And <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p2">why then</span> <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p3">would it be wrong to say</span> That <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w8">this world</span> is only <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w9">conceptions</span>. The <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p4">meaning of this verse</span>, according to the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w10">commentary</span>, is that none of the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w11">many worlds</span> that exist does so through some <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s230w12">essence of its own</span>: none of them are anything more than <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s230p5">products of our conception</span>.</span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; PROVISIONAL machine alignment proposed independently by Codex (English-first). The active English of 'jig rten ma rig rkyen can du is retained as a complete depth-3 recast rather than splitting rkyen can into an unsupported atom. The negative ma grub pa is omitted because its force is distributed across 'none ... does so' and cannot receive a truthful contiguous English atom without overlapping other mappings. C16:807 has identical ACIP/Wylie but projection vocabulary in English; this comparison does not establish independent publication lineage.</div>
